<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean bank says two Kia units seeking loans.</title>
<headline>S.Korean bank says two Kia units seeking loans.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Korea Development Bank said on Monday that two affiliates of the Kia Group were seeking loans of 30 billion won each.  </p>
<p>A bank official said Kia Steel had asked for 30 billion won to meet its operating expenses, while Kia Motors sought the same amount to finance facility investments.</p>
<p>&quot;Our bank has not yet decided whether to extend the loans,&quot; said the official.</p>
</text>
